## Project Overview

I built this SOC home lab to get more hands-on practice with security monitoring and investigation. 
I used Wazuh, Windows 11, Ubuntu Server, and VirtualBox to create a small lab where I can generate Windows activity,
collect logs, and see how that activity shows up in a SIEM. I also wanted to get better at troubleshooting when logs 
or alerts do not show up the way I expect.

## Environment

- Wazuh
- Windows 11
- Ubuntu Server
- VirtualBox
- VirtualBox Internal Network for communication between the Windows VM and Ubuntu server
- NAT adapter on Ubuntu for Internet access
- Ubuntu Server internal IP: 10.1.2.2
- Windows client IP: 10.1.2.10

## What I Configured

- Set up an Ubuntu Server VM and Windows 11 VM in VirtualBox
- Configured a private internal network between Ubuntu and Windows
- Set up DHCP on Ubuntu so the Windows VM could receive an IP address
- Installed and configured Wazuh on the Ubuntu server
- Connected the Windows endpoint to the Wazuh manager
- Configured Windows Task Scheduler Operational logs so Wazuh could collect that telemetry
- Enabled Wazuh raw event archiving for troubleshooting

## Security Activities

- Reviewed Windows security and Task Scheduler events in Event Viewer
- Tested scheduled task activity and checked what Windows events were generated
- Searched Wazuh Threat Hunting for the scheduled task and related Event IDs
- Investigated missing telemetry when expected events did not appear in Wazuh
- Verified the Wazuh agent was active and communicating with the manager
- Enabled Task Scheduler Operational logging and generated new events for testing
- Used Wazuh raw event archiving to help troubleshoot whether events were reaching the manager

## Current Challenge / Next Milestone

Right now I am troubleshooting whether Windows Task Scheduler Event ID 100 is actually reaching 
the Wazuh manager. Windows is generating the event and the Wazuh agent is connected, but I still 
need to confirm the event is being received on the manager side. My next step is to verify that 
first before moving on to custom detection rules, Sysmon, or another attack scenario.

## Skills Demonstrated

- SIEM monitoring with Wazuh
- Windows Event Viewer analysis
- Windows endpoint telemetry analysis
- Wazuh agent configuration
- Log collection troubleshooting
- Network troubleshooting
- Linux server administration
- Alert and event investigation
- Hypothesis-based troubleshooting
- Technical documentation
